<overview>
<p>The Capellan Confederation has always relied on its infantry to compensate for the CCAF's chronic shortage of heavier assets. Conventional foot soldiers, drawn from the citizens' militia system that defines Capellan military service, form the backbone of garrison forces across the Confederation's commonalities. Motorized platoons provide the CCAF with faster-moving infantry that can reposition between garrison posts or screen advancing forces along road networks. Their motorcycle and light vehicle transports sacrifice protection for speed, making them best suited to patrol and rapid-response roles. Armed with standard ballistic assault rifles, the most common and affordable infantry weapon in the Inner Sphere, these platoons deliver reliable short-range firepower and can be equipped and resupplied from almost any garrison stockpile. Trained as sappers, these platoons specialize in demolition, obstacle breaching, and field fortification work, giving commanders the ability to shape terrain and deny it to the enemy.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on introduction date of ballistic plate armor. Ballistic plate armor chosen for damage divisor and ATOW stats and general description.
</notes>

